            "description": "The FW Multi-Criteria Detector is designed to be connected to a two-wire SLC loop that provides both data and - VDC power. The detector is connected to the incoming and out going supply via terminals L and L in the mounting base A remote LED indicator may be connected between the R and R terminals. A ground connection terminal is also provided. The low profile design of the FW Multi-Criteria Detector is sleek and evolutionary, with a LED indicator which illuminates red when in alarm. At the heart of the photoelectric smoke sensor is Purelight Sensing Technology which incorporates Cone technology combined with a high-intensity infrared LED to provide stability and accurate sensitivity to smoke A sophisticated dynamic algorithm, providing transient re rejection and compensation for drift while maintaining accurate sensitivity.",
            "features": [
              "Approved to UL 7th edition and UL 521",
              "Internal drift compensation",
              "Easy installation",
              "Compatible with XP systems",
              "XPERT card addressing",
              "Built-in self-test",
              "Dual heat sensors",
